Article 6-2 (Implementation of Multisource Evaluations)
(1) The Minister of Justice may conduct multisource evaluations under Article 28 of the Regulations on Performance Evaluation, etc. of Public Officials for prosecutors at the senior prosecutor level (referring to chiefs of divisions and prosecutors at high prosecutors' offices; deputy chief prosecutors and chiefs of divisions at district prosecutors' offices; chiefs, deputy chief prosecutors, and chiefs of divisions at branch offices of district prosecutors' offices; prosecutors appointed as directors-general for planning, policy officers, officers in charge, spokespersons, or division directors at the Ministry of Justice or the Supreme Prosecutors' Office; and prosecutors holding positions designated by the Minister of Justice following deliberation by the Prosecutors' Personnel Committee under Article 35 (1) of the Act).
(2) Evaluators in multisource evaluations under paragraph (1) shall be the following persons:
1. Prosecutors of the rank of prosecutor of the Supreme Prosecutors' Office or higher;
2. Persons who passed the judicial examination and completed training at the Judicial Research and Training Institute in the same year as the prosecutor subject to multisource evaluation, or persons who passed the bar examination in the same year as that prosecutor;
3. Prosecutors who have served or are serving at the same prosecutors' office, branch office, or division as the prosecutor subject to multisource evaluation.
